## TDD: Streaming Support

Implement first-class streaming for LLM responses with backpressure and chunking.

### Red Phase - Write Failing Tests First
```typescript
// tests/ai/streaming.test.ts
import { ai, stream } from '@dotdo/ai'

test('stream() returns async iterable', async () => {
  const s = stream(ai`Tell me a story`)
  const chunks: string[] = []
  for await (const chunk of s) {
    chunks.push(chunk)
  }
  expect(chunks.length).toBeGreaterThan(1)
  expect(chunks.join('')).toBeTruthy()
})

test('stream supports ReadableStream', async () => {
  const readable = ai`Generate content`.toReadableStream()
  expect(readable).toBeInstanceOf(ReadableStream)
  const reader = readable.getReader()
  const { value } = await reader.read()
  expect(value).toBeDefined()
})

test('stream handles backpressure', async () => {
  const s = stream(ai`Long response`)
  let paused = false
  s.onBackpressure(() => { paused = true })
  // Simulate slow consumer
  for await (const chunk of s) {
    await delay(100)
  }
  expect(paused).toBe(true)
})

test('stream emits metadata on complete', async () => {
  const s = stream(ai`Short response`)
  let meta
  s.onComplete(m => { meta = m })
  for await (const _ of s) {}
  expect(meta.tokens).toBeDefined()
})
```

### Green Phase - Minimal Implementation
- Async generator wrapper for provider streams
- ReadableStream adapter for web APIs
- Backpressure signaling
- Metadata collection during streaming

### Refactor Phase
- Add stream combinators (map, filter, take)
- Optimize chunking strategy
- Reference: primitives/packages/ai-core for StreamingTextResponse

### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Failing tests written first
- [ ] AsyncIterator works with for-await-of
- [ ] ReadableStream adapter for fetch responses
- [ ] Backpressure handling prevents memory bloat
- [ ] Metadata available after stream completes

